  "notes": "A classically- and jazz-trained pianist whose documented method is a hybrid: he \"**fuses hip-hop sampling and drum programming with live instrumentation**\". The research gives his lane era as 1989–2010; **the window is trimmed to 1990–2010 here for Gate 2**, which excludes nothing the entry names. The band is \"70–100 straight\", marked `[LOW-CONF]`, with the mode at 88. Three drum deltas encode the hybrid directly: \"a programmed hip-hop kick/snare grid with live drums, live percussion and played instruments layered over it; backbeat flat on 2&4, sample-derived swing\" — so `swing.amount` is 0.60 (sample-derived, not programmed), `quantizeStrength` falls to 0.6 with the snare 4–9 ms off the grid, and the perc bed is five lanes (conga, bongo, tambourine, ride, shaker) at three to seven hits a bar, over a played 8th hat rather than a gridded 16th one. Harmony is the identifying parameter and it comes from the training — Howard University jazz on a classical childhood, \"extended and altered chords, real modulation\" — plus \"**his own string and horn arrangements**… 4-chord-plus cycles, gospel/jazz voice leading, horn stabs and string counterlines written rather than sampled\". So `maxChords` is 6, the triad share is 0.12, ninth is 0.38, a `vii°` passing family is authored with `susOrDimProb` raised, and the countermelody carries the written horns at a 0.54 density. The bass is \"played bass or a sampled bass line under a sub-kick; the low end is musical rather than sustained-808\", so `followRootsProb` is 0.56 with a six-wide passing-tone set and no `bass808` block. ⚠ Confidence is medium: the method, training and arranging roles are sourced but the tempo is inferred. ⚠ Every velocity and density number is INFERRED. ⚠ `session.keys` is INFERRED: the entry's Keys line gives \"jazz-piano harmonic language — Howard University jazz training on top of a classical childhood (Carnegie Hall and Brooklyn Academy of Music by 12)\" and enumerates no tonic, so the values here and their weights are this author's reading of that line.",
